 ],
 "digest": "This week's digest examines institutional arrangements that mediate Southern financial centres' integration into global networks. We review research on blended finance governance at Brazil's development bank, structural dependence in transnational finance, and terms-of-trade subordination across postcolonial Africa—establishing the conditions under which Southern centres function. Empirical work on liquidity integration in African exchanges and investor composition in Morocco's market, alongside coverage of Nigeria's pension mobilization for infrastructure and Cape Town's nature-bond innovation, illustrates how specific financial devices circulate through particular Southern institutions. We also note emerging payment infrastructure in Brazil, digital regulatory experiments, and comparative analyses of securities law—all material to understanding whether these arrangements consolidate subordination or enable functional alternatives."
}